[list]
[*]Fixed: a plutonium processor or reactor core built into a wall could resolve to the room on the wrong side of it. A building like that belongs to no room of its own, so the mod reads the cells around it, and when those fell evenly between two rooms it took whichever the game looked at first, which was always the southern or eastern side. The same build mirrored north to south quietly stopped working. An enclosed room now beats the outdoors, and a processor that genuinely faces two rooms equally arms neither rather than being right half the time.
[*]Fixed: a room holding both the nuclear machining table and the Rimatomics research bench armed for only one of them. A room takes one role and a research bench outscores a machining table, so the room came out a laboratory and the table's smithing work dressed nobody. Both benches are now read from the room's contents as well as from its role, so one room can hold both and arm for both.
[*]Fixed: the nuclear work type still read "Loading" for anyone not playing in English. The clearer name was there, but the mod only looked for it in the active language and it ships in English, so every other language fell back to the old unfindable label. It now falls back to the English one instead.
[*]Fixed: loading a missile silo or a railgun magazine looked beside the silo rather than beside the ammunition. Those jobs are built the same way round as the fuel loaders and the colonist walks to the round first. Both are hauling work, which no room turns on by itself, so it only shows on a stand you ticked for hauling by hand.
[*]The setup note was wrong and is corrected. A stand in the reactor hall does not cover fetching fuel, because a colonist changes where the job begins and a fuel run begins at the rods. Put a stand where the rods are kept as well as one in the hall.
[/list]
